Exercise 15:
•	Write a Bash script named security_log_analyser.sh.
nano security_log_analyser.sh 
•	The script should:
Accept a log filename as a command-line argument. Check whether the argument is provided.
Check whether the file exists. Extract failed login attempts. Extract invalid-user attempts.
Replace sensitive IP addresses with [REDACTED_IP]. Add the heading SECURITY ALERT REPORT.
Add [ALERT] before suspicious entries. Append END OF REPORT.
Save the result in security_alert_report.txt. Display the generated report.
 
#!/usr/bin/bash if [ $# -eq 0 ] then
echo "Error: Please provide a log filename." exit 1
fi
if [ ! -f "$1" ] then
echo "Error: File does not exist." exit 1
fi
echo "SECURITY ALERT REPORT" > security_alert_report.txt sed -n \
-e '/Failed password/p' \
-e '/Invalid user/p' "$1" |
sed -E 's/[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+/[REDACTED_IP]/g' |
sed 's/^/[ALERT] /' >> security_alert_report.txt
echo "END OF REPORT" >> security_alert_report.txt cat security_alert_report.txt
